    <h2 style="margin-top:0">The discount, in plain numbers</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Monthly plan:</strong> $150/month instead of $175/month. $0 down. Discount applies for the entire duration of the engagement &mdash; not just the first year. <strong>That is $300/year saved, every year you stay.</strong></li>
      <li><strong>Lump-sum plan:</strong> $3,500 instead of $4,000 for a full custom-coded site, ownership transferred to you on launch.</li>
      <li><strong>Free 5-point audit either way.</strong> If you are not ready to build yet, the <a href="/audit/" class="inline-link">free audit</a> is also free, and I will mark you flagged for the discount the day you do hire me.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Who qualifies</h2>
    <p>Anyone with verifiable U.S. or Canadian military service, plus their immediate family:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Active duty (any branch &mdash; Army, Navy, Marines, Air Force, Space Force, Coast Guard, U.S. Public Health Service, NOAA Corps, Canadian Armed Forces).</li>
      <li>Reserves and National Guard / Reserve Force.</li>
      <li>Honorably discharged veterans, regardless of length of service.</li>
      <li>Retired military.</li>
      <li>Service-connected disabled veterans.</li>
      <li><strong>Spouses, children, parents, and siblings</strong> of any of the above. The same discount, same verification (one shared photo of the service member's documentation, plus a one-line note identifying the relationship).</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>How verification works:</strong> One photo or scan of any of the following &mdash; DD-214, Veteran ID Card (VIC), VA ID, military ID (with sensitive numbers redacted is fine), state DMV-issued veteran-designated driver's license, or Canadian Armed Forces / Veterans Affairs Canada documentation. Email it once when we start; I delete the file the moment I confirm. I do not retain copies of your documents.</p>

    <h2>How to claim it</h2>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Book a 20-minute discovery call.</strong> <a href="/contact/" class="inline-link">Standard contact form</a>. In the message, mention you are claiming the veterans discount.</li>
      <li><strong>On the call, we figure out the build.</strong> Same call I do with anyone &mdash; what your business needs, what kind of site fits, which plan makes sense.</li>
      <li><strong>Send proof of service.</strong> One photo of any qualifying document, by email. Takes you 30 seconds.</li>
      <li><strong>I apply the discount on day one.</strong> Your first invoice is at the discounted rate, not the standard rate. There is no "ramp" or "after first year" reset.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Why I do this</h2>
    <p>Two reasons. First, my immediate family and several close friends are veterans. The discount is a small, concrete way of saying thank you. Second, a meaningful share of small service-business owners in the U.S. and Canada are veterans &mdash; the trades you operate in (HVAC, plumbing, electrical, roofing, inspection, landscaping, contracting) overlap heavily with post-service careers. If a $25/month or $500 lump-sum gap is the difference between you having a real website and not, that is a gap worth closing.</p>

